<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<addon
  id="pvr.sublime"
  version="@ADDON_VERSION@"
  name="Sublime TV"
  provider-name="patkino (pvr.tvlink by Alex@ELEC)">
  <requires>@ADDON_DEPENDS@
  </requires>
  <extension
    point="kodi.pvrclient"
    library_@PLATFORM_LIB@="@LIBRARY_FILENAME@"/>
  <extension point="xbmc.addon.metadata">
    <platform>@PLATFORM_TAG@</platform>
    <license>GPL-2.0-or-later</license>
    <source>https://github.com/patkino2022/pvr.sublime</source>
    <summary lang="en_GB">TV client for service.tvlink</summary>
    <summary lang="ru_RU">ТВ-клиент для service.tvlink</summary>
    <description lang="en_GB">Live TV, archive and guide from the service.tvlink add-on. Based on pvr.tvlink by Alex@ELEC; does not depend on the AlexELEC image.</description>
    <description lang="ru_RU">Прямой эфир, архив и телегид из дополнения service.tvlink. Основан на pvr.tvlink от Alex@ELEC и не зависит от образа AlexELEC.</description>
    <assets>
      <icon>icon.png</icon>
    </assets>
    <news>
v22.1.4
- Settings: fields service.tvlink always overwrites are hidden (still defined)
v22.1.3
- DASH channels (#KODIPROP:inputstream=inputstream.adaptive from service.tvlink) play through inputstream.adaptive
v22.1.2
- Live stream read without Kodi's stream buffer: channel switch no longer waits for the next segment
v22.1.1
- Instance created by the add-on class: survives Kodi creating the client twice (was "Not implemented")
v22.1.0
- pvr.sublime: own id, built outside the AlexELEC image
- Startup: retry the playlist until the server answers (was: wait for the next refresh hour)
v22.0.6
- Epg: add parsed EPG-cache binary file
v22.0.5
- Epg: optimize download xmltv-file based on TVLINK xmltv.status
v22.0.4
- Del: option Use FFmpeg playlist
v22.0.3
- Set: one option Use Inputstream FFmpeg Direct
v22.0.2
- Add: always play EPG Tags as live-stream
v22.0.1
- Fix: Timeshift/Catchup
v22.0.0
- Init: first version for Kodi-22 (Piers)
    </news>
  </extension>
</addon>
